<title>TURKEY: Turkish Emlak to sign $100-mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Turkish Emlak to sign $100-mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's state-owned Emlakbank will sign an agreement next week for a $100-million two-year syndicated loan, arranged by Bankers Trust, Dai-Ichi Kangyo bank and Fuji Bank, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the fully-written pre-export financing facility would have a margin of 75 basis points over Libor.</p>
<p>The agreement will be signed on November 6 in London.</p>
</text>
